# Frozen row truth (the closed plan's 「存放与冻结」, `git show 423458df:docs/plans/asr-row-truth-plan.md`),
#   2026-10-12. sha256sum format; lines starting with # are notes.
# Every path is relative to the main checkout's data/diarization/row-truth/ (not tracked):
#   cd data/diarization/row-truth && sha256sum -c <this file>
# Rulers:
#   dev-v2-high: prompt v2 (no asr field), Gemini 3.8 Flash high, the five dev windows' six correction windows.
#   heldout-v3-high: prompt v3, Gemini 3.8 Flash high, the six held-out windows' seven correction windows; built once.
# Prompts are pinned by commit, not hashed here (the templates move on): v2 = the templates and row_truth.py's
#   MATERIALS / CAVEATS / LABELS at e0774bb0, v3 = at 23cfb40f. v2 -> v3 adds only the asr field and its example
#   rows; the speaker rules and the per-material text are the same, so the two sets' speaker fields are comparable.
# Products scored against them (copied from tmp/diarization-retrack/ on 2026-10-12):
#   products/acoustic/<ident>/: the acceptance run's stable (production's acoustic cells) and its correction plan;
#   products/sol/, products/luna/: the aligned judge runs (GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Luna), stable and speaker-judge sidecar.
# external-v4-text-high (2026-10-13): the integrated models' dedicated rulers, one per (window, output), text-only
#   variant of prompt v4 (row_truth_text_system.md / row_truth_text_example.md and row_truth_external.py at 423458df),
#   Gemini 3.8 Flash high; each file carries the rows it judged (rows_shown), so it scores without the model outputs.
# external-judge-high (2026-10-13): round 9's judge (agy Gemini 3.8 Flash high) on the integrated models' rows
#   (row_truth_external_judge.py at bff4b478, the commit that froze them): text/ MOSS Pro on all eleven windows and 35t 300 s,
#   MAI2 on hina-24, hina-47, manosaba-c; audio/ the three models on those three windows.
# inputs/ (2026-10-13): every file the readouts read from the main checkout's tmp/ and out/ (the acceptance runs'
#   stables, diar sidecars and correction plans, round 8/9's window lists and round 9's agy answers, the p2 feature
#   caches round 9's loader reads, the phase-1 medium rulers and the LLM mapping review), at its path there. Each
#   readout starts with row_truth.ready(), which puts a missing one back and refuses one that differs; found by tracing
#   every file the readouts open. products/acoustic/ is the same acceptance stable and plan, kept as frozen with the rulers.
